Now Tomcat receives:

GET /student

But Tomcat has many Servlets.

How does it know which Servlet should handle /student?

That's Servlet Mapping.

@WebServlet("/student")
public class StudentServlet extends HttpServlet {
}

This means:

/student
     ↓
StudentServlet

So:

http://localhost:8080/student

will go to:

StudentServlet


Older XML way

You could also configure it in web.xml:

<servlet>
    <servlet-name>student</servlet-name>
    <servlet-class>StudentServlet</servlet-class>
</servlet>

<servlet-mapping>
    <servlet-name>student</servlet-name>
    <url-pattern>/student</url-pattern>
</servlet-mapping>

Modern Java applications generally use annotations instead.
